=== P2 Shared surface 0167 Breadcrumbs (Windows) ===

SURFACE: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/Breadcrumbs/Breadcrumbs.{cs,Model.cs,ViewModel.cs}
WEB SOURCE: web/src/components/layout/Breadcrumbs.tsx  (layout-chrome breadcrumb trail, presentational)
TESTS: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/SharedSurfaces/BreadcrumbsTests.cs (41 headless test cases)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY NOTES (web -> native)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Composition: the web source renders a <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"> as an inline flex row (gap-1,
  overflow-x-auto scrollbar-none) with a leading Home icon link followed by chevron-separated crumbs. The
  native surface mirrors that with a ScrollViewer (horizontal, scrollbar hidden, vertical disabled) hosting a
  horizontal StackPanel (Spacing=4): a leading Home HyperlinkButton (Segoe Fluent Home glyph \uE80F), then per
  crumb a ChevronRight FontIcon (\uE76C) + the crumb element. It composes WinUI primitives + the shared
  Components/DataDisplay DisplayTokens brushes per Windows HIG; the atomic crumb primitive (Components/Layout
  TsBreadcrumbs) is the P2 component-library bundle and out of scope here.
- Data sources (web hooks -> native seams): the ONLY web hook is useTranslation -> ILocalizer (P1/S10). The
  web component is presentational - `items` / `homeHref` / `homeAriaLabel` are props the parent owns and it
  delegates each link's navigation + hover/focus prefetch to <PrefetchLink>. The native IBreadcrumbNavigator
  (P1/S8 seam) plays PrefetchLink's role (Navigate / Prefetch); items flow in through SetItems and are
  projected by the UI-thread-free BreadcrumbsViewModel. The view performs no I/O, i18n, projection or routing
  of its own - it binds the holder.
- States reproduced (every branch the web source actually renders):
    * collapsed  -> web `if (items.length <= 1) return null`; the native surface hides itself (Visibility=
                    Collapsed) for a 0/1-crumb trail, matching the web empty-slot behaviour exactly (the
                    LayoutBreadcrumbs contract: top-level pages render nothing). Reproduced, not invented.
    * populated  -> Home link + chevron-separated crumbs.
    * current    -> trailing crumb (isLast) renders as TextSecondary + font-medium text, never a link, even
                    when it carries an href (web `isLast || !item.href`).
    * link       -> a non-last crumb with an href renders as a muted HyperlinkButton (web PrefetchLink).
    * text       -> a non-last crumb without an href renders as muted text (web span).
    * middle     -> interior crumbs collapse on a narrow viewport and a per-crumb horizontal-ellipsis (\u2026,
                    aria-hidden) is shown instead (web `hidden sm:inline` / `sm:hidden`, sm=640px), driven by
                    SizeChanged + the pure BreadcrumbResponsive.IsNarrow decision.
  The web Breadcrumbs is a presentational layout control fed by props with NO data fetch, so it has NO loading
  / error / stale / offline chrome - and none is invented (honesty covenant: no drift in either direction; the
  same reasoning the predecessor SkipToContent / RouteAnnouncer / SortControl surfaces logged).
- i18n (web t() keys -> P1/S10): both keys ALREADY exist in the catalog (no resw change needed), verified in
  en/ar/he (2/2 each): translation.a11y.breadcrumb "Breadcrumb" (nav landmark name) and
  translation.a11y.breadcrumbHome "Dashboard" (Home link name). No English literals in native code; every
  visible/accessible string flows through ILocalizer + BreadcrumbsRegistration fallbacks (verbatim from the
  web t() second args), with the homeAriaLabel prop override honored.
- Accessibility: the surface is an AutomationLandmarkType.Navigation landmark carrying the localized
  "Breadcrumb" name (web <nav aria-label>); the Home link carries the localized "Dashboard" Narrator name (web
  aria-label, explicit homeAriaLabel honored); each crumb link/text carries its label; the collapsed-ellipsis
  is AccessibilityView.Raw (web aria-hidden="true"); labels truncate at 200px (web max-w-[200px]). Inherits
  WinUI hover/pressed/focus visuals, Narrator support and system font scaling from HyperlinkButton. No
  animation -> reduced-motion is a non-issue.
- Diagnostics (P1/S11): emits `view.opened slug=Breadcrumbs` once on Loaded (idempotent). PII-safe (slug only;
  never a crumb label or an href - an href can carry fleet ids like /charging/{id} - asserted by a leak test).

